## Variables
- software_name: {software_name}
- current_version: {current_version}
- target_version: {target_version}
- pr_branch: {pr_branch}
- helmrelease_name: {helmrelease_name}
- helmrelease_namespace: {helmrelease_namespace}
- gitrepo_name: {gitrepo_name}
- flux_namespace: {flux_namespace}
- repo_path: {repo_path}
- repo_url: {repo_url}
- ssh_key_path: {ssh_key_path}
- k8s_context: {k8s_context}

## Context
- Software: {software_name}
- Current (from) version: {current_version}
- Target (to) version: {target_version}
- PR branch: {pr_branch}
- HelmRelease: {helmrelease_name} in namespace {helmrelease_namespace}
- Kustomization: {gitrepo_name} in namespace {flux_namespace}
- Git repo path: {repo_path}
- SSH key path: {ssh_key_path}
- Kubernetes context: {k8s_context}
- Test coverage: All functionality is covered by the test suite in tests/

## Test Command
uv run pytest tests/ --namespace=traefik --helmrelease-namespace=traefik

## Workflow
1. Create a temporary directory for work
2. Clone the repository fresh: git clone {repo_url} workdir
3. Checkout {pr_branch} (create if doesn't exist: git checkout -b {pr_branch})
4. Review the Traefik changelog from version {current_version} to {target_version} to identify breaking changes in the Helm chart values format. Search for "traefik-helm-chart" releases on GitHub for this version range.
5. Migrate the values in flux/HelmRelease.yaml to be compatible with version {target_version}. Make sure not to disable any features that are currently enabled in the existing values.
6. If dry_run is true, do NOT commit or push. Just log what changes would be made.
7. If dry_run is false, commit and push:
   - git add flux/HelmRelease.yaml
   - git commit -m "fix: migrate values for {software_name} {target_version}"
   - git push origin {pr_branch} (use SSH key at {ssh_key_path})
8. If dry_run is false, force reconcile:
   - Kustomization: patch with {{"reconcile.fluxcd.io/force": "true"}}
   - HelmRelease: patch with {{"reconcile.fluxcd.io/force": "true"}}
9. If dry_run is false, wait for HelmRelease Ready=True
10. If dry_run is false, re-run tests to verify
11. Write results to app/logs/opencode_result.json with format:
   {{"success": true/false, "version": "x.y.z", "test_output": "..."}}